repo modernization
  keep the CI action pins current; recheck on each push and bump when
    GitHub deprecates a runtime (r-lib/actions stays @v2, the latest
    major).
  sanitizer follow-ups: a gcc-asan/valgrind variant, and gating the
    sanitizers workflow on pull_request once it has proven stable.
  the equivalence gate could ride CI but needs its statistical
    (z-score) mode wired cross-platform - the bitwise baselines are
    ARM-recorded.
  codecov CI wiring remains optional if a public badge is ever wanted
    (coverage is measured locally on demand; 88 percent at last run).
  optional, larger, taste-dependent: roxygen2 migration (hand-written
    Rd is complete and codoc-clean today; migration buys inline
    doc-next-to-code at the cost of a huge one-time diff); NEWS.md
    instead of inst/NEWS.Rd (pkgdown renders it natively).

decision-gated (design notes in docs/design/)
  integer-weight probit (post 1.0): Phi(f)^w is exactly tractable as w
    replicated latent draws - the tree side stays O(n) because the
    latent mean is a sufficient statistic (zbar_i ~ N(f_i, 1/w_i),
    the existing weighted-gaussian machinery); only the latent-update
    phase scales as Theta(sum w_i), i.e. linear in the UNAGGREGATED
    count, which silently undoes the aggregation that motivates count
    weights. The shipped weighted logistic has the same structure
    (fbd2168 draws PG(w, psi) as a sum of w PG(1, psi) variates), so
    replication would not be a regression - both families are exact
    but linear in total counts. If large counts ever matter, the
    standard fix is a threshold hybrid: exact summation for small w,
    a large-w approximation above it (CLT normal approximation for
    the truncated-normal sum; Windle et al. large-b Polya-Gamma
    samplers) - O(1) per observation but perturbs the stationary
    distribution, so it must be a deliberate, documented switch.
  arbitrary real logistic weights: needs a general real-shape PG
    sampler; the survey/IPW use case wants it but is a
    pseudo-likelihood trap (see docs/design/weighted-logistic.md).
  sampled gp lengthscales: gp-leaves.md stage-4 addendum - needs a
    theta prior choice, per-sample theta channels in state/flatten
    formats, and costs multiples of the draw phase per sweep; not the
    mechanical follow-up the original proposal suggested.
  public group.by exposure beyond rbart_vi: grouped-random-effects.md;
    naming reserved.

consumer-gated
  sparse extensions (sparse-columns.md landing notes): in-place
    mutation, sparse x.test, u8 per-column widths, streaming range
    kernel, mutation on dense-backed mixed columns
  low-rank gp kernels
  score-to-draw chol(V) reuse within a sweep (measured second-order
